{{also|Poliomyelitis}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Poliomyelitis}}, from the {{etyl|grc|en}} {{affix|grc|πολιός|t1=grey|μυελός|t2=marrow|-ῖτις|t3={{l|en|-itis}}|nocat=1}}. Compare the {{cog|fr|poliomyélite}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{enPR|pŏ'lĭōmīəlīʹtĭs|pō'lĭōmīəlīʹtĭs}}, {{IPA|/ˌpɒlɪəʊmaɪəˈlaɪtɪs/|/ˈpəʊlɪəʊmaɪəˈlaɪtɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|poliomyelitides}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} Acute infection by the [[poliovirus]], especially of the [[motor neuron]]s in the [[spinal cord]] and [[brainstem]], leading to muscle weakness, [[paralysis]] and sometimes deformity.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|infantile paralysis}}, {{l|en|polio}}

